<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea LG Chemical buys Indian firm.</title>
<headline>S.Korea LG Chemical buys Indian firm.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>LG Chemical Co Ltd, a unit of South Korea's LG Group, said on Tuesday it had taken over India's largest polystyrene maker Hindustan Polymers for $35 million.  </p>
<p>LG Chemical said in a statement the decision to buy the Indian firm was part of its drive to expand overseas business.</p>
<p>&quot;Major chemical companies are seen advancing into India. We need to set up a bridgehead there before anyone else,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>LG Chemical plans to increase its overseas production to about half of its total production in 2005 from the current 20 percent, it said.</p>
</text>
